{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003442-question-about-spirits-in-the-near-realms","id":1003442,"title":"Question about spirits in the Near Realms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-15T09:30:57-08:00","id":1003442,"title":"Question about spirits in the Near Realms","content":"I'm reading the Velvet Shadow book for W20, and when it gets to talking about the Near Realms the spirits there start to closely resemble actual people/animals at times. I'm going to use Pangea as an example. There are tribes of humans living in that Realm, as well as different breeds of animals from all through out history. My question is, mechanically, are they still spirits? If a fight were to break out, do they all do Agg damage, and have Essence and charms?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:02:29-08:00","id":1003456,"title":"","content":"Personally, I've treated them as &quot;normal&quot; animals/people for the sake of physical stats and health levels. I treat all emanations that way.<br /> Whether or not I've had them deal Agg has changed depending on the needs of the story (though I stay consistent within any given story) and the creature in question. For example, deer use normal stats for deer, but a T-rex might very well do Agg. <br /> <br /> That being said, which gifts work on them is a bit fuzzy imo. They can usually be affected by gifts that affect spirits. Though that can heavily depend on the Gift (I would use Beast speech instead of Spirit speech to talk to them for example).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:27:37-08:00","id":1003727,"title":"","content":"My $.02 : Remember that emanations are <i>not</i>, strictly speaking, spirits. They're emanations <i>of a</i> spirit realm. In essence an extension of the realm itself, not distinct entities. Now they can <i>mimic</i> sentience, but in the strictest sense, they are not sentient beings. Now there are exceptions, for instance Charys in Erebus -- but that actually is a spirit (an Incarna, I believe) and not an emanation. So for emanations, I would say that &quot;normal&quot; animals/people who use physical stats (as per idpersona's example), Gifts would work on them as they would on a physical being, while more robust emanations that do Aggravated damage and would have more spirit-like stats, Gifts that affect spirits would be needed. I'd just use the rule of thumb that many of the realms are intended to mimic the physical realm (Battleground, for instance) and others more spirit-like realms (Legendary Realm, for instance) and <i>that </i>should be the primary factor for influencing how &quot;physical&quot; or &quot;spiritual&quot; your emanations behave in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T21:30:07-08:00","id":1003773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003442-question-about-spirits-in-the-near-realms?p=1003727#post1003727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My $.02 : Remember that emanations are <i>not</i>, strictly speaking, spirits. They're emanations <i>of a</i> spirit realm. In essence an extension of the realm itself, not distinct entities. Now they can <i>mimic</i> sentience, but in the strictest sense, they are not sentient beings. Now there are exceptions, for instance Charys in Erebus -- but that actually is a spirit (an Incarna, I believe) and not an emanation. So for emanations, I would say that &quot;normal&quot; animals/people who use physical stats (as per idpersona's example), Gifts would work on them as they would on a physical being, while more robust emanations that do Aggravated damage and would have more spirit-like stats, Gifts that affect spirits would be needed. I'd just use the rule of thumb that many of the realms are intended to mimic the physical realm (Battleground, for instance) and others more spirit-like realms (Legendary Realm, for instance) and <i>that </i>should be the primary factor for influencing how &quot;physical&quot; or &quot;spiritual&quot; your emanations behave in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of funny, at least to me. After the previous thread, when I saw you commented (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3506_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3506\" data-vbnamecard=\"3506\">Uniform Two Six</a> ), I sighed and clicked to see what was stated here. But I actually agree with pretty much 100% of what's said above.<br /> I don't think an emanation doing Agg should automatically require more spirit-like stats, but I can see how that approach might be taken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T22:37:07-08:00","id":1003787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1003442-question-about-spirits-in-the-near-realms?p=1003773#post1003773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of funny, at least to me. After the previous thread, when I saw you commented (<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3506_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3506\" data-vbnamecard=\"3506\">Uniform Two Six</a> ), I sighed and clicked to see what was stated here. But I actually agree with pretty much 100% of what's said above.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMeh... You know what they say; Even a broken clock is right twice a day.<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think an emanation doing Agg should automatically require more spirit-like stats, but I can see how that approach might be taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I still think it's a good rule of thumb, but I'd concede exceptions to it. An emanation that appears as a Garou would plausibly do aggravated damage, but still use physical stats, as an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T07:52:08-08:00","id":1003935,"title":"","content":"They are spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11698-darko","name":"Darko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11698_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}